<title>ITALY: Reno De Medici plans eurolira bond issue.</title>
<headline>Reno De Medici plans eurolira bond issue.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian cardboard maker Reno de Medici, listed on the Milan bourse since July, said it plans to launch a variable rate eurobond for a value of between 100 and 150 billion lire.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the issue, indexed to LIBOR, was likely to be launched by the end of February by R.D.M. International, its recently created Luxemburg unit.</p>
<p>The loan will provide financial resources for the group's programme of development over the next few years. -- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
